4. SIMD extensions

Upstream accelerates most of the codec with SIMD extensions (simd/), which it
builds by default (WITH_SIMD) for the targets it supports. This package
currently builds them only on x86-64, where they are NASM sources assembled
with the nasm package (a build-time dependency) and simd/jsimd.c selects SSE2
or AVX2 at run time. On other targets, or with config.libjpeg_turbo.simd=false,
the library uses upstream's C code paths, as it does when SIMD is unavailable.

The Arm Neon extensions (simd/arm/) are C intrinsics and need no new
dependency. The i386 ones (simd/i386/) are NASM sources, like x86-64.
